# Supabase connection (Vite only reads VITE_* — restart dev after changing).
# Get these from the Sinsay Supabase project dashboard → Project Settings → API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL= 
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY= 
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY= 
# Live tables expected by src/lib/queries.ts + staff-auth.ts (migration 030):
#   to_staff, operator_applications, payment_transactions,
#   dive_pass_inventory, tourists
# Private storage bucket for receipt uploads (signed URLs, 1h TTL):
#   operator_uploads
# NOTE: VITE_* vars are baked at build time (see vite.config.ts). On Vercel,
# set them as Environment Variables BEFORE `bun run build`, then redeploy
# after any rotation.

# CARTO Basemaps API key (free tier) — required since Sep 2026 or raster
# tiles render an "API key required" watermark. Request one at
# https://carto.com/basemaps/apikey (email only, no account) and set the
# real value in .env (local) + Vercel env vars (deploys). Without a key the
# heatmap falls back to plain OpenStreetMap tiles.
# VITE_CARTO_KEY=

# Server-only (NEVER VITE_-prefixed, NEVER committed with a real value).
# Powers src/server/create-staff.ts (superadmin staff creation). Set in the
# shell for local dev (`export SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=...`) and in Vercel
# → Project → Settings → Environment Variables for deploys. Anyone holding
# this key bypasses ALL row-level security — treat it like a password.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Public origin of THIS dashboard, used to build the password-reset link's
# redirectTo (src/lib/request-staff-reset-fn.ts). Also add the resulting URL
# (<origin>/reset-password) to Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration
# → Redirect URLs, or Supabase silently falls back to the Site URL and the
# emailed link lands on the dashboard instead of the password page.
# Server-side only, so SITE_URL works too; falls back to http://localhost:8080.
# SITE_URL=
